hadiths[68]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1822",") Hadith (1844 Ayyub bin Saeed narrates that I offered a funeral prayer following the example of Sayyiduna Zaid bin Arqam, and he recited five takbeers. Then he narrated that I offered a funeral prayer following the example of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he also recited five takbeers. Therefore, we will not abandon them because of any person."
"1823","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said six takbirs on the people of Badr, five takbirs on the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and four takbirs on all other people."
"1824","Narrator named Marqa narrates that I performed a funeral prayer following the example of Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam, and he recited Takbeer five times during it."
"1825","Isa, the slave of Sayyidna Huzaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I performed a funeral prayer under the guidance of my master (Sayyidna Huzaifa bin Yaman, may God be pleased with him), who was a good man, and he recited the takbeer five times. was"
"1826","Ubaid bin Saaq narrates that once Sayyiduna Sahl bin Haneef (RA) led us in the funeral prayer, when he said the first takbeer, then he recited Surah Fatiha until his voice reached the people behind him. The narrator narrates, then he continued to say Takbeer until there was only one Takbeer left, so he recited the words of Tashahhud for the prayer, then he said Takbeer and ended the prayer."
"1827","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came back after attending the funeral of a person in the field of Baqi', I was feeling a severe pain in my head. (The literal translation of this would be: Oh! I died.) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Oh, my head! Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""If you die before me, you will not suffer any harm because I will give you a shroud, I will perform your funeral prayer, and I will bury you."" When you do that, you will come back to my house and spend the night here with your new wife.' The Prophet smiled. After that, the suffering of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began, in which he passed away."
"1828","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: ""So I will give you a bath and I will give you a shroud."""
"1829","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission and it has these words ""So I will bathe you."""
"1830","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed a funeral prayer, then he (PBUH) placed his blessed right hand on his blessed left hand."
"1831","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform the funeral prayer for a person, he (peace be upon him) would raise both hands in the first takbeer and then place his blessed right hand on his blessed left hand."
"1832","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise both hands in the first takbeer of the funeral prayer, and after that he did not raise his hands while saying the takbeer in the funeral prayer."
"1833","According to Umarubian, a Christian woman died who had a Muslim child in her womb, so Sayyiduna Umar (RA) ordered that this woman should be buried in the Muslim cemetery because of the child."
"1834","Abu Salman narrates that once Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, led the funeral prayer of a person, and he recited Takbeer five times. So they said it was done on purpose, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pay it in the same way."
"1835","Abdullah Bin Ka'b narrates this statement of his father, Sayyidna Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. He said that his mother, who was a Christian, had passed away and he wanted to attend the funeral of his mother. (Imam Darqutni, may God have mercy on him) narrates this hadith is not proven. One of the narrators of this hadith is weak."
"1836","Abdullah bin Aamir narrates this statement of his father. I remember this very well about the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he buried Sayyidna Uthman bin Mazoon, may Allah be pleased with him. They were standing on the side."
"1837","Masrooq narrates that Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, led the funeral prayer of a wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I heard him say, ""I will offer the funeral prayer for this woman in the same way that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the funeral prayer for the last time."""
"1838","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) did not raise both hands while praying, he used to raise both hands so much that the whiteness of his armpits could be seen."
"1839","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When you bathe the dead, it is not necessary for you to bathe because your dead body is not najis. That is sufficient for you. Wash your hands."
"1840","Imam Shaabi narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave whose owner had been buried some time ago. The narrator narrates: I asked Imam Shaabi: Who narrated this hadith to you? He replied that it was narrated by a reliable person, who was present on this occasion, that is Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA)."
"1841","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave that was isolated, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Takbeer four times over it (while performing the funeral prayer). The same hadith has been narrated along with some other isnads and all these narrators have narrated the same thing."
"1842","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led a funeral prayer for a person."
"1843","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man used to clean the mosque (of the Prophet) 'He passed away and was buried at night'. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and others with him visited the grave of that person. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “These graves are filled with darkness for their people (i.e. men), and Allah, the Exalted, illuminates their graves for them because of my offering the funeral prayer of these people.” These words of tradition are from a narrator named Ali bin Muslim."
"1844","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) visited the grave of a person after he was buried. There are these words in a hadith: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed (the funeral prayer) on the grave of a woman."
"1845","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) saw a newly built grave and asked why you did not tell me about it. The people said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sleeping at that time. We did not like to wake him up. Some narrators have quoted some additional words and meanings in it, but the meaning is the same."
"1846","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered his funeral prayer three days after the death of a person."
"1847","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered the funeral prayer at the grave of a person one month after his burial. The narrator named Bishrban Adam is unique in quoting from the narrator named Abu Asim."
"1848","Sayyiduna Abu Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the nine men who participated in the Battle of Uhud were brought, and with them was the tenth Sayyidna Hamzah (may God be pleased with them). Then these nine people were buried and Sayyidna Hamza (RA) was not buried (meaning the Prophet (PBUH) performed the funeral prayer of Sayyidna Hamza (RA)."
"1849","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed the funeral prayers of those who were martyred in the Battle of Uhud after eight years."
"1850","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jafar (RA) narrates that when the news of the death of Sayyidna Ja'far Tayyar (RA) came, the Prophet (PBUH) said, ""Prepare food for Ja'far's family, as a situation has befallen them which has preoccupied them (the narrator is in doubt about a word here)."
"1851","Sayyidah Asma bint Umays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Sayyida Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) willed that her husband Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with her) and Asma (daughter of Umays) would bathe her, so they both gave her ghusl."
"1852","Nafee narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) led the funeral prayer for seven people together, including men and women. The narrator narrates that Sayyida Umm Kulthum, the wife of Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) and the daughter of Sayyidna Ali (RA) and her daughter-in-law were buried. His son's name was Zaid bin Umar. In those days, Sayyidna Saeed bin Al-Aas was the governor and among those present were Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, Abu Hurairah, Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri and Sayyidna Qatadah. I wonder what the method is? He said it is Sunnah."
"1853","Sayyiduna Utban bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered Nawafil in his house at the time of Chasht. Chapter: It is permissible to act a little during the prayer, and which prayer must be made up for the person who faints."
"1854","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray, 'If someone knocked on the door during that time, if the door was in front of him or on the right or left side of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Prophet (peace be upon him) would open the door."
"1855","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying and the door would be closed. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned that the door was in the direction of Qiblah."
"1856","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I used to ask to open the door, even though the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was performing Nawafil standing at that time."
"1857","Asim bin Zamra narrates: We said to Sayyiduna Ali (RA): Tell us a hadith about the Nawafil of the Prophet (PBUH)' So he said: 'Who can keep his strength'? The narrator says: 'We asked you to tell us about it as far as we have power, and we will perform it.' It would rise as much in the direction as Asr (rises in the direction of the west) then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform two rak'ats, and you would send salutations on the angels, the prophets and their followers, the believers and the Muslims in between them, then you would wait until at the time of Chasht, it would be so high that it would be as high as it was in the direction of the east at the time of Zuhr. If it was late, you would pray four rak'ahs and in them you would greet the angels, the prophets and their followers, the believers and the Muslims. After that, you would pray two rak'ahs (Sunnah) after the Zuhr prayer, and then you would pray four rak'ahs (Sunnah) before you, and you would also pray between them in the same way."
"1858","Asim Ibn Zamra narrated, 'We asked Sayyiduna Ali (RA) about the prayer of the Prophet (PBUH), and he said, 'Who has the power to do it?' That the sun would be as far away from the point of sunrise as it would be away from the point of sunset (i.e. it would be the time of sunset). At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform four rak'ahs of Sunnah before the Zuhr prayer after sunset, then he would perform two rak'ahs of Sunnah after Zuhr, and then he would perform the first four rak'ahs again."
"1859","Yazid, the slave of Sayyidna Ammar (RA) narrates that once Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) fell into a stupor, which lasted until the time of Zuhr Asr (Maghrib) and Isha."
"1860","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a person who faints and leaves the prayer. If he comes, that person will perform this prayer. The words of both the narrators of this tradition are the same, but there is some difference in the chain of transmission."
"1861","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, that once he was unconscious for a day and a night, and he did not make up the prayers during that time."
"1862","According to another chain of transmission, it has been narrated that once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) was unconscious for more than two days, so he did not make up the prayers (during that time)."
"1863","Nafee narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was once unconscious for three days and three nights, so he did not make up (the obligatory prayers) during that time."
"1864","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to look left and right while praying, but he did not turn his neck and look at his back. A narrator named Fazl bin Musa is unique in narrating this tradition as a connected tradition. Other rabbis have quoted it as a mursal tradition."
"1865","Abdullah bin Saeed narrates this in his chain of transmission: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to look here and there during the prayer without bending his neck."
"1866","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this (in order to attract the Imam): The command to say Subhan Allah is for men and the command to clap is for women."
"1867","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever makes a gesture during the prayer that is understood, then that person will perform his prayer again. One of the narrators of this hadith is unknown, and the last part of the hadith is an addition to the hadith. It may be. These are the words of the narrator. It is authentically proven from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to point during prayer. This hadith has been narrated by Sayyidna Anas, Sayyidna Jabir (RA) and other Companions of the Prophet (RA) with reference to the Prophet (PBUH)."
"1868","Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to make gestures while praying."
"1869","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to make gestures while praying."
"1870","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever performs one prostration of the morning prayer before the sun rises, he performs this prayer, or if he performs the prostration (of the Asr prayer) before the sun sets, he performs this prayer."
"1871","Bakir bin Ashaj states that there were nine mosques in Madinah along with the blessed mosque of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). During the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the people living near these mosques used to listen to the adhan of Sayyiduna Bilal (may God be pleased with them), but they used to pray in these mosques. There was a mosque of Banu Salama, a mosque of Banurataj, which belonged to Banu Abd al-Ashhal, a mosque of Banuzareq, a mosque of Banughafar, a mosque of Islam and a mosque of Jahina, the narrator has doubts about the ninth mosque. Chapter - A person who prays facing another person who is looking in front of him in the direction of the Qibla, must pray again."
"1872","Muhammad bin Hanafiya narrated that the Holy Prophet saw a person who was praying towards another person, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that person to pray again. I have performed the complete prayer for you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""You have performed the prayer in such a state that you were looking at another person in the direction of the Qiblah."""
"1873","Sayyidna Abbas Jashmi narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said that some imams are people who drive away. Qatadah, the narrator of this tradition, says, ""According to my knowledge, those who drive away here are those who recite for a long time during Ma'mat until people leave them and go away."""
"1874","Ibn Sabat narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the morning prayer, he recited seven verses in it, then he heard the sound of a child crying, so he went into ruku', then he stood up (in the second rak'at), then he recited two verses and went into ruku'."
"1875","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes hear the cry of a child with its mother."
"1876","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said to me that you should not expose your breasts in front of anyone and do not look at the breasts of any living or deceased person (because the breasts are a hundredfold)."
"1877","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had a muezzin who used to give adhan in the manner of Tarbiyah."
"1878","Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a person who performs four rak'ats after the Isha prayer, recites them, bows and prostrates well in them, then that person will get the same reward for this prayer as the reward for performing those rak'ats in Shab al-Qadr."
"1879","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that menstruating and puerperal women should not recite any part of the Qur'an."
"1880","Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajra (RA) narrates that a blind person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I hear the call to prayer, but sometimes there is no one to accompany me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""When you hear the call to prayer, accept the invitation of the person calling you to Allah (i.e., come to the mosque to pray in congregation)."
"1881","Sayyidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) forbade the imam standing on top of something and the people behind him are called narrators, that is, those standing below him on the ground."
"1882","Sayyidna Abu Murshad Ghanwi, may Allah be pleased with him, who had the honor of participating in the Battle of Badr, narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that if you want your prayer to be accepted, let your best people lead you because they are the representatives between you and your Lord. The authenticity of this tradition is not proven. The narrator of this tradition, Abdullah bin Musa, is weak."
"1883","Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said this when those people bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Sayyidna Muhammad (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) is the Messenger of Allah, and those people establish prayer, and pay Zakat, then they will secure their lives and their wealth from me. It will be the responsibility (then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Radiyallahu Anhu said) By Allah! If those people refuse to pay me a rope that they used to pay to the Holy Prophet, then I will fight with them on that too."
"1884","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: I have been commanded to do three things. I have been commanded to fight with the people until they confess that there is no god but Allah. It will be the responsibility of Allah."
"1885","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight with people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, to establish prayer, and to pay Zakat."
"1886","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: I have been ordered to fight with the people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah. The right will remain intact and the account of these people will be held by Allah Ta'ala."
"1887","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat is not required on a person's wealth until a year has passed. Other narrators have narrated it as a suspended tradition."
"1888","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Zakat is not required on the benefited property until one year has passed on it."
"1889","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Zakat on wealth is not required until one year has passed. The narrators have differed in quoting some words here."
